tty: send full-range RGB to a screen that says it takes it

The driver's Broadcast RGB, left at Automatic, sends limited-range RGB
for a TV mode such as 3840x2160 at 60 Hz, and a monitor reading full
range shows its blacks grey. With NIRI_FULL_RANGE_WHEN_SELECTABLE=1 in
its environment, niri sets Broadcast RGB to Full on a connector whose
EDID says, in a CTA video capability block, that its RGB range is
selectable, so the AVI infoframe tells the screen it's sent full range.
A screen that says nothing, such as a TV that wants limited range, is
left at Automatic. It's asked through the environment rather than the
config, so a config written for this niri still parses in one without
the patch.

